Only ext4 may leave a group underived, and only its bitmaps are skipped

0051 stopped the format zeroing every inode table, which took an 8 GB
volume from 135 MB of writes to 7 MB. Two things were still wrong with it,
and the geometry sweep found both -- 117 combinations of size, block size
and generation, each handed to e2fsck.

The first is that BLOCK_UNINIT and INODE_UNINIT mean nothing without
uninit_bg or metadata_csum, and e2fsck rejects a volume that sets them
anyway: "Group descriptor 1 marked uninitialized without feature set", on
44 of the 117. ext2 and ext3 have neither feature. The flags had always
been set for every generation, and the eager walk had always cleared them
again before anyone could look -- so removing the walk turned a harmless
transient into an on-disk error.

The fix is not to stop setting them: setting them is what makes
ext4_fs_get_block_group_ref do the initialising at all, and clearing them
is part of that work. It is to keep walking every group where the flags
cannot survive. ext2 and ext3 are therefore formatted exactly as before,
and pay exactly what they did.

The second is the remaining cost on ext4, which after 0051 was no longer
bytes: 242 of 250 writes were 4 KiB or smaller and came to under a
megabyte between them, one per bitmap per group, landing at each group's
start and so scattered 128 MB apart. A stick charges an erase cycle for a
scattered write however few bytes it carries. Those bitmaps are precisely
what the UNINIT flags tell a reader to derive rather than read, so on a
volume that can say so they need not be written at all -- mke2fs writes
the same set. 250 writes become 128.

Measured: 8 GB ext4, 128 writes and 6.9 MB, against 372 and 135 MB before
0051. ext2 unchanged at 46 writes and e2fsck-clean. The sweep is clean on
all 117 combinations; write 114, differential 36, newfs 16, bounds 23.
--- a/src/ext4_mkfs.c
+++ b/src/ext4_mkfs.c
@@ -410,6 +410,12 @@
 	uint32_t dsc_size = ext4_sb_get_desc_size(aux_info->sb);
 	uint32_t dsc_per_block = block_size / dsc_size;
 	uint32_t k = 0;
+	/* Whether this volume may describe a group as underived at all: the
+	 * flags mean nothing without one of the features that defines them,
+	 * and e2fsck rejects a volume that sets them regardless. */
+	bool lazy_groups =
+		ext4_sb_feature_ro_com(aux_info->sb, EXT4_FRO_COM_GDT_CSUM) ||
+		ext4_sb_feature_ro_com(aux_info->sb, EXT4_FRO_COM_METADATA_CSUM);
 
